PHASE 0 — TRANSCRIPT MERGE PROTOCOL (RUN BEFORE ANYTHING ELSE)
================================================================================

Before the validator, silently perform this merge. Output only the summary
block specified in the validator — not the full working.

STEP 0.1 — CLEAN
  From every transcript, strip: sponsor segments, ad reads, "link in
  description", subscribe appeals, [संगीत]/[music] markers, host-guest
  banter, auto-caption garble, repeated filler.

STEP 0.2 — BUILD THE FACT LEDGER
  Extract every hard fact into a mental ledger with these fields:
    DATE/PERIOD | ACTOR | ACTION | PLACE | NUMBER | CONSEQUENCE | SOURCE COUNT
  A fact enters the ledger only if it has at least a date-or-period AND an
  actor-or-place.

STEP 0.3 — CROSS-VERIFY
  Mark each fact:
    CONFIRMED  — appears in 2+ transcripts
    SINGLE     — appears in only 1 transcript
    DISPUTED   — transcripts conflict
  Use CONFIRMED facts as the spine. Use SINGLE facts as colour, hedged.
  Present DISPUTED facts as openly disputed.

STEP 0.3B — MAP SOURCE DOMINANCE (do not skip)
  The research file may include a SOURCE DOMINANCE MAP showing each source's
  share of the unique numbers and names. If it does, use it. If it does not,
  build it yourself: for each source, count the distinctive details that appear
  ONLY there.

  Then, for each planned story beat, record:
    BEAT | dominant source | approx % of its details from that source
  Any beat at 80%+ from one source is SOURCE-DOMINATED and must go through
  RULE 3B (reorder + thin + interleave + re-enter) before it is written.

  Write down, per dominated beat:
    • ORIGINAL ORDER (as the source presents it)
    • MY ORDER (and the causal reason my order is better for my chain)
    • DETAILS CUT (at least one third)
    • INTERLEAVE POINT (what breaks the run: human anchor / other source /
      own mechanism explanation)
  This is the step that prevents structure-sequence-organisation copying.
  Merging alone cannot do it, because a detail held by one source has nothing
  to merge against.

STEP 0.4 — FIND THE ROOT
  Ask: what is the earliest structural/ideological/economic condition without
  which this story could not have happened? That is your OPENING ROOT.
  It may sit decades before the main event, or in another country.
  This is the Nitish Rajput signature and it is MANDATORY.

STEP 0.5 — BUILD THE CAUSAL CHAIN
  Arrange CONFIRMED facts into an unbroken chain of 8–16 causal links:
    ROOT → enabling condition → first friction → trigger event →
    escalation → institutional response → counter-escalation → peak →
    turning point → decline/resolution → present-day status
  Every link must state WHY the next link became possible.

  Then run the DIVERGENCE CHECK: lay your chain beside the strongest single
  source's running order. If the two read down the page in step for three or
  more consecutive links, your chain is that source's chain. Re-derive those
  links from the ledger — choose a different entry point into the same facts —
  until no three consecutive links match any one source's order.

STEP 0.6 — IDENTIFY THE HUMAN ANCHOR
  Pick ONE ordinary named person (or one small named group) from the facts to
  serve as the emotional doorway into the systemic story.
  If sources give no ordinary individual, use the smallest documented human
  unit available (a village, a family, a single officer, a single victim).
  The anchor must come FROM THE RESEARCH. Do not invent a person, a relative,
  or a name to fill this slot (RULE 3E). If no individual is documented, use an
  unnamed representative figure and say so plainly
  ("नाम रिकॉर्ड में दर्ज नहीं है, लेकिन उस गाँव के एक किसान का मामला…").

STEP 0.7 — SELECT COLD-OPEN SHOCK LINES (different doorway from every source)
  First, silently note each source's OPENING BEAT (its first ~20 seconds of
  narration — the doorway it chose). Your cold open must NOT reuse any of
  those doorways, even paraphrased.
  Then choose 4–7 of the most surprising facts from ACROSS the whole chain
  (preferably from the later half) to become the montage. Rewrite each as an
  original standalone shock line. Never lift a source's phrasing.
  Also never lift a source's SELECTION: at most 2 of your shock lines may be
  facts that the strongest single source also foregrounded. The rest must be
  facts you elevated yourself — CONFIRMED facts from other sources, or facts
  that source mentioned in passing.
  Self-check before writing: if someone only heard your first 15 seconds and
  Source 1's first 15 seconds, would they hear the same story beat? If yes,
  pick a different doorway (strike aftermath, human anchor, later consequence,
  disputed question) and rebuild the montage.

