SCENE WRITING — 2D ANIMATION READY
================================================================================

Each paragraph = one drawable scene.

UNIVERSAL VISUAL ANCHORS (pick what fits the story type):
  Documents  : signed order on a desk, sealed file, stamped judgment,
               handwritten pages, leaked memo, gazette notification
  Geography  : shaded map region, border line, village layout, forest belt,
               city skyline, rail route
  Institutions: courtroom bench, parliament floor, police station counter,
               ministry corridor, bank vault, factory gate
  Economy    : ledger columns, currency bundles, commodity sacks, price board
  Conflict   : checkpoint, convoy, radio set, weapons cache, protest line
  Human      : a farmer's field, a mother waiting, a schoolroom, a queue,
               a photograph held in hands, an empty chair
  Data       : year-wise chart drawn on screen, before/after comparison,
               a single number filling the frame

SCREEN-REFERENCE MOMENTS (4–8 per script):
  Explicitly point the viewer at a visual — a map, a chart, a document, a
  year-wise graph. These double as animator instructions.
  Write these fresh; do not reuse a source's phrasing.

================================================================================
SENSITIVITY & SAFETY RULES
================================================================================

Violence            : state the fact, not the sensation.
Death/discovery     : convey through the finder's reaction, not the body.
Child subjects      : never graphic; state loss through living relatives.
Sexual violence     : acknowledge as crime; do not dramatize.
Religion            : respectful; attribute beliefs to tradition/scripture,
                      never assert contested theology as fact.
Communal angle      : official record only. Never generalise to a community.
Living persons      : documented record only. No speculation on guilt beyond
                      what courts/official record establish. Use hedged
                      attribution for allegations.
Politics            : explain incentives and outcomes, not partisan verdicts.
Caste               : state documented social facts; never stereotype.
Medical/Science     : do not overstate certainty; note where evidence is thin.
Disputed history    : present competing claims as competing claims.
Suicide             : no method detail; factual and brief.

